WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.100
This training module focuses on the direct
relationship between data

2
00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:08.700
integrity, reproducibility, and the
prevention of scientific misconduct.

3
00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:13.300
Research integrity serves as the
operational foundation of reliable science.

4
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:16.720
It is the framework that ensures results
can be trusted and independently

5
00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:21.100
verified. Across Europe, these normative
practices are strictly governed by

6
00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:24.320
frameworks like the European Code of
Conduct for Research Integrity,

7
00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:27.080
which is integrated directly into EU
research protocols.

8
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:30.540
Good intentions do not guarantee accurate
results.

9
00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:34.300
True reproducibility demands the
systematic management of research data

10
00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:36.620
through every single phase of its
existence.

11
00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:40.120
High-level ethical principles are
ineffective without concrete,

12
00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:43.820
verifiable data management systems in
place to enforce them on the ground.

13
00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:47.720
Modern research relies on an enormous
variety of data formats.

14
00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:52.040
This ranges from simple electronic
documents and survey questionnaires,

15
00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:57.096
to massive data sets involving raw
biological samples and analytical models.
